conbody.p:
The following syntax block shows the structure of a PIVOT
      operation:SELECT columns FROM table_name
        PIVOT (
        aggregate_function_1(target_column) [as alias_1], aggregate_function_2(target_column) [as alias_2], ...
        FOR header_column IN (value_1 [AS alias_1], value_2 [AS alias_2], ...)
        ) [AS result_alias];

The following example shows a PIVOT operation that uses a
        count
      aggregation:SELECT year, v1, v2 FROM functional_parquet.alltypestiny PIVOT (
count(distinct month) FOR month IN (1 AS v1, 2 AS v2)
) AS t;

conbody.codeblock:
WITH t1 (a, b) AS (
VALUES (1, 2), (3, 4)
)
SELECT a, v2, v4 FROM t1 PIVOT (
min(b) FOR b IN (2 AS v2, 4 AS v4)
) AS t;
